c-like presentation with shock and RUQ pain."], "evidence_against": ["These factors are more typical of chronic liver disease (B5) than acute hepatic venous obstruction (B3), but B3 remains possible in the acute decompensation ph…"], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B3.1", "B3.2", "B3.3"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.5, "interrupt_relevance": 0.6, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": ["Budd-Chiari syndrome", "hepatic vein thrombosis"]}, "B4": {"id": "B4", "label": "Acute Inflammatory Abdominal Process", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.054, "danger": 0.5, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Lack of inflammatory markers (fever, leukocytosis) reduces the likelihood of B4 (inflammatory causes) and strengthens hemorrhagic etiologies (B1)."]}, "B5": {"id": "B5", "label": "Chronic Liver Disease with Acute De-compensation", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "reopened", "prior": 0.05, "posterior": 0.05434782608695651, "danger": 0.7, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 3.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.3, "interrupt_relevance": 0.2, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "time_course", "representative_diseases": ["Budd-Chiari syndrome", "cirrhosis with portal hypertension", "chronic Budd-Chiari"]}, "B1.1": {"id": "B1.1", "label": "Ectopic Pregnancy with Hemoperitoneum", "parent": "B1", "level": 2, "status": "live", "prior": 0.16304347826086954, "posterior": 0.16304347826086954, "danger": 0.9, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.6, "interrupt_r